{"name":"Sunday Niqab","hex":"#3d4035","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"niqab","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A veil which covers the face (except for the eyes), worn by some Muslim women as a part of sartorial hijab."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/niqab"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunday","blocks":[{"text":"Sunday is the day of the week between Saturday and Monday. Sunday is a day of rest in most Western countries and a part of the weekend. In some Arab countries, Sunday is a weekday."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday"},{"title":"Niqab","blocks":[{"text":"A niqāb, niqab, or niqaab, also known as a ruband, rubandah (روبنده) or  'qab (colloquial), is a long garment worn by some Muslim women, in order to cover their entire body and face, excluding their eyes. It is an interpretation in Islam of the concept of hijab, and is worn in public and in all other places where a woman may encounter non-mahram men. Most prevalent in the Arabian Peninsula, the niqab is a controversial clothing item in many parts of the world, including in some Muslim-majority countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Young_Muslim_Woman_on_Street_-_Sylhet_-_Bangladesh_%2812968288153%29.jpg/330px-Young_Muslim_Woman_on_Street_-_Sylhet_-_Bangladesh_%2812968288153%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niqab"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn